;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-13, for Phase 17 step 3 (design section
;; 19.7, proposal 3, approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-13. It replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-10,
;; whose Open, Flush, Char, String, Ln, Int and Hex this one keeps
;; unchanged. Why this is right:
;; - Err now imports FormattedText too, so its initializer calls
;;   FORMATTEDTEXT_INIT after LINEOUTPUT_INIT, then FindConsole.
;; - IsConsole is an exported BOOLEAN ("::"). FindConsole copies
;;   "SYS$ERROR" (MOVC5, 9 bytes, zero-filled to 16) and calls
;;   POC_IS_TERMINAL, Platform's routine ($GETDVIW, DVI$_DEVCLASS
;;   DC$_TERM), with its address and length 9, and sets IsConsole when
;;   R0 is 1.
;; - Ten passes e as a longword (CVTWL) to FORMATTEDTEXT_TEN and returns
;;   its G_floating result in R0 and R1; a function that reached its END
;;   would trap (12).
;; - Real copies its REAL argument (MOVF) and n, has FORMATTEDTEXT_REAL
;;   write the text into a 32-byte local (FormattedText.maxText), then
;;   Field writes n minus its length (FORMATTEDTEXT_LENGTH) blanks, then
;;   the text, through LINEOUTPUT_CHAR and LINEOUTPUT_STRING. LongReal is
;;   the same with the LONGREAL passed as the address of a copy (MOVG).
;; - On the guest, vax-out-reals' errtest prints llvm-err's output on
;;   SYS$ERROR as on standard error, and IsConsole is FALSE with
;;   SYS$ERROR in a file.
